## Why This Is Asked
 Tests ability to design a scalable, multi-tenant privacy enforcement and incident response workflow on GCP, including data lineage, per-tenant isolation, and automated remediation under real-time load.

## Key Concepts
 - Real-time data processing, per-tenant isolation, data masking, DLP, Vertex AI, Dataflow, Pub/Sub, Data Catalog lineage
 - Event-time vs processing-time semantics, idempotency, backpressure, rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function maskPII(record){
  const r = { ...record };
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-****';
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{1})(.*)(@)/, '$1***$2$3');
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the anomaly model under bursty traffic and schema drift?
- How would you handle false positives/negatives and post-incident cleanup?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a privacy-aware, multi-region data pipeline with governance and testing in a realistic setting.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming
- Multi-tenant masking and isolation
- CMEK and DLP integration
- Data Catalog lineage
- Schema evolution and backfills
- Two-region resilience and audits

## Code Example
```javascript
// Dataflow DoFn: mask PII based on tenant policy
class MaskPII {
  process(record, ctx) {
    const policy = getPolicy(ctx.tenantId);
    return maskRecord(record, policy);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test end-to-end lineage accuracy? 
- How would you handle policy updates without downtime?
